<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 47,378 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 47,378 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 47,378 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 72,349 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 8,015	    16,746</p>
<p>    Import cargo			39,363	    55,603</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and seven berthed.</p>
<p>In the next 24 hours, four ships were expected to sail and four were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 25,000	 Al-Safa		13/7</p>
<p>Gas oil		  27,000	 Sand Gate	    13/7</p>
<p>Crude oil		67,000	 Johar		  15/7</p>
<p>Palm oil		  5,800	 Wawasan Megah	16/7</p>
<p>Tallow		    3,020	 Trade Wind Express 14/7</p>
<p>Gas oil		   7,697	 Themera		 due</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,000	 Tae Dong Gang	 due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
